{"ref":"BDB, בַּקְבֻק","hw":"בַּקְבֻק","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">בַּקְבֻק</span></big>  <strong>n.</strong>[<strong>m.</strong>] <strong>flask (</strong>from gurgling sound of emptying, cf. Arabic <span dir=\"rtl\">بَقْبَقَةٌ</span> <em>gurgling sound;</em> also Syriac <span dir=\"rtl\">ܒܰܓܒܽܘܓܳܐ</span>, <em>cantharus</em> etc.<strong>)</strong>—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּקְבֻּק</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 19:10\" href=\"/Jeremiah.19.10\">Je 19:10</a>; cstr. <em>id.</em> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 14:3\" href=\"/I_Kings.14.3\">1 K 14:3</a> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 19:1\" href=\"/Jeremiah.19.1\">Je 19:1</a>.","next":"BDB, בַּקְבּוּק²","prev":"BDB, בָּקַק²"}